          <type><ref refid="classMR_1_1Const__RasterLoadSettings" kindref="compound">MR.Const_RasterLoadSettings</ref>?</type>
          <declname>settings</declname>
          <defval>null</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>loads the first image of a .tiff file as a raster with one layer: </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>gray, palette and RGB images keep the stored samples of any type (gray values, color indices or color components) as channels;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>libtiff decodes the other formats (gray with alpha, YCbCr, CMYK, less than 8 bits per sample, etc.) to four UInt8 channels of RGBA colors, which are not multiplied by alpha unless the file stores them so (associated alpha);</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the formats that libtiff cannot decode are read as stored too if each pixel has one sample or three or more interleaved samples of 8 to 64 bits, otherwise loading fails;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the files compressed by the methods that libtiff does not support fail to load;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the rows keep the stored order whatever the Orientation tag says, also in the decoded formats Generated from function <computeroutput><ref refid="classMR_1_1RasterLoad_1a2cf02b499f72beaa678019f2a03f22f5" kindref="member">MR.RasterLoad.fromTiff</ref></computeroutput>. Parameter <computeroutput>settings</computeroutput> defaults to <computeroutput>{}</computeroutput>. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
